BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260728T031715Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53497609947661
DTSTART:20260922T200000Z
DTEND:20260922T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to thrive at NC State? If so\, join the African A
 merican Cultural Center (AACC) for the fall EQUIP Academic Workshop. The w
 orkshop is designed to help first-year students master the academic transi
 tion to NC State. Co-facilitated with campus partners and peer leaders\, t
 his interactive session will focus on practical skills\, such as college-l
 evel study strategies\, major exploration\, syllabus navigation and buildi
 ng effective relationships with faculty and advisors. The session will als
 o include:\n\nAn interactive mini-workshop: Get real-world tips\, tricks a
 nd time-management strategies from Academic Success Center experts.Group d
 iscussion: Chat with your peers\, share what’s working and what’s not 
 and build a toolkit together.What I Wish I Knew student panel: Hear unfilt
 ered advice\, honest stories and proven study hacks from experienced stude
 nt leaders who have been in your shoes.You'll leave with real strategies\,
  better habits and a connection to student leaders.\n\nComplete the regist
 ration form to save your spot. Contact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director
  of the AACC\, at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Roo
 m 356)
SUMMARY:EQUIP Academic Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-academic-workshop
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260728T031715Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53391555009737
DTSTART:20260925T180000Z
DTEND:20260925T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center as it celebrates Hara
 mbee! and 55 years of the African American Cultural Center and its legacy 
 of fostering community\, connection and student success at NC State.\n\nHa
 rambee! is designed to connect the Wolfpack community with a wide array of
  resources and services available on and off campus. By strengthening rela
 tionships across the university and beyond\, the program promotes academic
  achievement and personal growth.\n\nTogether\, we will celebrate our shar
 ed commitment to excellence\, belonging and community.
GEO:35.785221;-78.675064
LOCATION:Harris Field
SUMMARY:Harambee!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/harambee-9582
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260728T031715Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53497726461438
DTSTART:20261015T213000Z
DTEND:20261015T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center for our fall Learning
  Labs. This dynamic workshop series is designed to help students build ski
 lls and explore their creativity. Each hands-on session is a supportive sp
 ace for you to connect with peers\, learn from passionate facilitators and
  grow your talents. \n\nOur Oct. 15 workshop will introduce the basics of 
 mixing\, Serato functions and other fundamentals related to the art of DJi
 ng. Participants will have the opportunity to play with Pioneer DJ control
 lers that we borrowed through the NC State University Libraries Tech Lendi
 ng program. For more information about the controllers\, visit the Librari
 es website.\n\nThis workshop is intended as an introduction to DJing\, but
  it's open to individuals of all skill sets. Please contact Andaiye Qaasim
 \, assistant director of the African American Cultural Center\, at aaqaasi
 m@ncsu.edu if you have questions about the lab.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Sec
 ond-Floor Gallery)
SUMMARY:Learning Lab: DJ 101
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/learning-lab-dj-101
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260728T031715Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53374549856476
DTSTART:20261022T213000Z
DTEND:20261022T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to thrive at NC State? If so\, join the African A
 merican Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP Fall Wellness Workshop. EQUIP
  is a year-long initiative that will support first-year students as they c
 ultivate self-awareness\, resilience and community. Grounded in social-emo
 tional learning\, EQUIP's psychoeducational workshops empower first-year s
 tudents to cultivate self-awareness\, personal agency and emotional intell
 igence as they navigate college rigor. This interactive session will cover
  common first-year challenges\, including academic stress\, identity devel
 opment and help-seeking habits. Through structured reflection\, scenario e
 xploration and peer modeling\, participants will build vital skills in res
 ilience and proactive resource engagement to thrive inside and outside the
  classroom.\n\nIf you have questions about EQUIP or the session\, contact 
 Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director of AACC\, at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Roo
 m 356)
SUMMARY:EQUIP Fall Wellness Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-fall-wellness-workshop
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
