BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260728T031715Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53496362193327
DTSTART:20270211T140000Z
DTEND:20270212T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:The African American Cultural Center and our campus partners in
 vite the university community and the public to our annual Symposium on Af
 rofuturism and Diasporic Scholarship. Our focus this year connects to our 
 55th anniversary and the theme of Legacy\, Libations and Liberation. \n\nT
 he symposium will feature African diasporic learning\, scholarship and epi
 stemologies via cutting-edge research\, storytelling\, creative works\, di
 scussion circles\, community-based projects and industry initiatives from 
 the NC State and the surrounding community. The symposium will include ora
 l presentations\, roundtables\, poster presentations\, creative practices\
 , keynote speakers\, panels and networking opportunities. \n\nWe welcome s
 ubmissions to present at the conference from students\, staff\, faculty\, 
 alumni\, community members and surrounding university and college partners
 . For a full description of the symposium\, including information on submi
 tting a proposal\, visit our website.
GEO:35.769292;-78.676638
LOCATION:James B. Hunt Jr. Library\, Various Spaces
SUMMARY:Symposium on Afrofuturism and Diasporic Scholarship
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/symposium-on-afrofuturism-and
 -diasporic-scholarship-8461
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
